  "query_preview": "..Gusty southwest winds continue over the eastern half \nof our CWA this afternoon, the Wind Advisory for Apache County has \nbeen extended through the end of the day. Much drier and stable air \nhas moved into the western zones and this will move east across the \nCWA through the day and into Tuesday. The band of shallow moisture \nfrom earlier this morning is slowly mixing out and shower chances \nhave essentially reached zero.\n\nThe remainder of the week will feature a slow and steady rise in \ntemperatures, dry conditions and typical southwesterly winds each \nafternoon. A weak trough does persist over the area through at least \nFriday, so some of those afternoon gusts may have a little extra \nspeed at times, but nothing impactful.\n\nBy next weekend, ridging forms over the area and we should expect \ntemperatures to rise a bit above normal as a result. However, it \nstill looks very dry.",
